WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.415
An internet address identifies a network endpoint for routing,

00:00:03.415 --> 00:00:07.225
but public address ownership and application control are different concepts.

00:00:07.225 --> 00:00:11.240
Registry data may associate an address range with a network operator, cloud provider,

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.350
content-delivery network, or hosting company.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.265
Cloud platforms allocate and reassign addresses.

00:00:16.265 --> 00:00:19.480
Shared hosting places multiple customers on the same infrastructure.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.280
Content-delivery networks and reverse proxies present provider addresses while shielding

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.280
an origin.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.080
Managed security services may also stand between users and the application.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.600
These layers make simple attribution unreliable.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.920
An address observed in DNS does not automatically identify the organization operating the

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.695
application,

00:00:35.695 --> 00:00:39.215
the physical server location, or the party responsible for an event.

00:00:39.215 --> 00:00:43.465
Additional domain, certificate, provider, timing, and internal evidence is required.

00:00:43.465 --> 00:00:46.600
Geolocation databases estimate location and can disagree.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.090
They may identify a provider office, registration country, network hub,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.080
or outdated assignment rather than the system's physical position.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.244
Report geolocation as an estimate with source and date, not as a precise fact.

00:00:57.244 --> 00:00:59.580
Hosting context remains useful for defensive work.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.220
It can reveal external dependencies, concentration risk, provider changes,

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:04.610
unrecognized public assets,

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:08.435
or infrastructure that should be reconciled with contracts and inventories.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:11.200
Document observed addresses, source dates, provider context,

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.880
shared-infrastructure limitations, and confidence.

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.040
Avoid intrusive probing or access attempts.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.430
Escalate questions through authorized asset owners and vendors so public indicators are

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:22.110
validated against operational records.
